            ; ── CLAIMED 2026-08-03, after model-discovery.fk stopped testing filenames. ──────────
            ; The registry had 35 rows and this host had 22 GGUF files; the difference was not
            ; models nobody had bothered to write down, it was models nothing could SEE. Discovery
            ; asked `.gguf` of a name, and ollama stores every model it pulls as
            ; ~/.ollama/models/blobs/sha256-<64 hex> with no extension at all — including the blob
            ; base.llama32-3b-metal has been decoding tokens from since 2026-07-21. Sixteen models
            ; were invisible for the length of a string comparison.
            ;
            ; WHAT THE DIGEST IN THESE ROWS IS. An ollama blob's FILENAME is the sha256 of its own
            ; bytes; that is what content-addressed storage means and it was verified here rather
            ; than assumed — `shasum -a 256` on sha256-970aa74c… (nomic) and on sha256-dde5aa3f…
            ; (the champion) both reproduced their own names on 2026-08-03. So these artifact fields
            ; are real digests, not labels, and each row can be re-checked against its file in one
            ; command. What they are NOT is a measurement: every one of these rows is `observed`,
            ; score 0, samples 0. Present on disk, read by its own header, unmeasured against
            ; anything. The registry's rule holds — a local artifact is welcome immediately, and its
            ; name never grants authority.
            (nmcp-model "challenger.kat-coder-v25-metal" "general-code-agent" "text" "local-native" "component" "partial" "native-recipe" "fkwu+Metal" "KAT-Coder-V2.5-Dev-Compact" "5f5fcf953b2b5757de8eabb11d9770c2d9d280a7723d67f7ad654629f8f45dda" "not-locally-trained" "receipts/2026-08-03-selfnamed.md; metal_kat_exit.sh VERDICT PASS 2026-08-03 argmax id=3637 wall 1.175s; kat-coder-{embed,layer-shape,pipeline-map,tensor-table} and gated-deltanet-{layer,conv,gates} bands all green 2026-08-03" "exit-path-mechanism-witness" 0 0 0 45 "run the 41 blocks between entrance and exit — 30 gated-deltanet plus 11 full-attention — so the argmax is fed a hidden state and not an embedding" 20260803 30 0 0 1 0)
            (nmcp-model "base.llama33-70b-local" "general-text" "text" "local-native" "shadow" "observed" "local-process" "ollama" "llama3.3:70b" "4824460d29f2058aaf6e1118a63a7a197a09bed509f0e7d4e2efb1ee273b447d" "not-locally-trained" "receipts/2026-08-03-selfnamed.md; own header read 2026-08-03: llama, 80 blocks" "unmeasured-on-sealed-task" 0 0 0 18 "measure on a sealed paired task or retire the pull" 20260803 7 0 0 0 0)
            (nmcp-model "base.qwen25-72b-local" "general-text" "text" "local-native" "shadow" "observed" "local-process" "ollama" "qwen2.5:72b" "6e7fdda508e91cb0f63de5c15ff79ac63a1584ccafd751c07ca12b7f442101b8" "not-locally-trained" "receipts/2026-08-03-selfnamed.md; own header read 2026-08-03: qwen2, 80 blocks" "unmeasured-on-sealed-task" 0 0 0 17 "measure on a sealed paired task or retire the pull" 20260803 7 0 0 0 0)
            (nmcp-model "base.qwen25-coder-32b-local" "general-text-code" "text" "local-native" "shadow" "observed" "local-process" "ollama" "coder:latest" "67f5470b8d17b37fb49e76ad797dd6eda93997499c3031aa33a6ac3f77804668" "not-locally-trained" "receipts/2026-08-03-selfnamed.md; own header read 2026-08-03: qwen2, 64 blocks, general.name Qwen2.5 Coder 32B Instruct AWQ" "unmeasured-on-sealed-task" 0 0 0 22 "compare against the KAT and ds4 code lanes on one sealed paired task" 20260803 7 0 0 0 0)
            (nmcp-model "base.deepseek-r1-32b-local" "general-reasoning" "text" "local-native" "shadow" "observed" "local-process" "ollama" "deepseek-r1:32b" "6150cb382311b69f09cc0f9a1b69fc029cbd742b66bb8ec531aa5ecf5c613e93" "not-locally-trained" "receipts/2026-08-03-selfnamed.md; own header read 2026-08-03: qwen2, 64 blocks" "unmeasured-on-sealed-task" 0 0 0 16 "measure on a sealed paired task or retire the pull" 20260803 7 0 0 0 0)
